`14 x 14 = 196` ordered label pairs reconstruct the same two local fidelities
and the same `q=1/4`.

All 24 distinct proper cubic rotation matrices have determinant `+1`, are
orthogonal, and rotate the fronts, outcome labels, target shift, and physical
factor maps together. Every rotated witness remains clean and has the same
exact commutator. Translation covariance is symbolic: adding arbitrary
`(tau_x,tau_y,tau_z)` to all anchors, targets, factor sites, and carrier sites
leaves every relative coordinate and both shared-site intersections unchanged.

Two negative controls prevent a blanket overlap claim:

- an exact shared-target pair has `q=1` and commutes; and
- far-disjoint controls have no shared factors, `q=1`, and factorize.

The wall is partial radial overlap with `0<q<1`, not overlap or multiplicity in
general.

